# AppModule Client Relationships

`src/Web/ClientApp/src/app/app.module.ts` is the entry-point record for the client's existing TypeScript module. Start by retaining the adjacent imports at the top of the file; when revisiting the old client wiring, starting here is more reliable than guessing relationships from module names.

```ts
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { APP_ID, NgModule } from '@angular/core';
```

The browser platform and Angular core each have an import, with `APP_ID` and `NgModule` in the same core declaration. Forms and routing follow immediately:

```ts
import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';
import { RouterModule } from '@angular/router';
```

These four are the direct dependencies currently visible at the top of the file.
